        "notes": "RIGOR (reported, not fixed \u2014 the defect is numeric/nomenclature). (1) 'E_mol = m_e alpha^2 / 2 supplies the Hartree energy scale' names the wrong atomic unit. The Hartree is E_h = alpha^2 m_e c^2 = 27.2113862 eV; the quantity written, alpha^2 m_e c^2 / 2 = 13.6056931 eV, is the RYDBERG (recomputed at m_e c^2 = 0.51099895069 MeV, alpha^{-1} = 137.035999177). Either drop the factor 1/2 to make the name right, or call it the Rydberg. The factor of two propagates into every E_bond the proposition predicts, so this is not cosmetic. (2) The closing claim that multiple inverse trefoils drive 'the 1 : 2 : 3 bond-energy scaling' does not match measured bond energies: C-C 348, C=C 614, C\u2261C 839 kJ/mol is 1 : 1.76 : 2.41, and N-N/N=N/N\u2261N (163/418/941) is 1 : 2.56 : 5.77. No common bond family scales 1 : 2 : 3, so the claim needs either a citation for where 1 : 2 : 3 is observed or restatement as the bare multiplier count."
      }
